.env
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
.git/
# `data/*`, NOT `data/` -- .vercelignore uses .gitignore semantics, so an excluded
# DIRECTORY is never descended into and a negation inside it is never evaluated. This was
# got right in .gitignore and left wrong here, and the deploy fell back to the database
# silently: /api/health reported source="database" on production while every local check
# said "snapshot". That `source` field is the only reason it was visible at all.
data/*
# [A107] The one file in data/ the deployment needs: without it the function silently falls
# back to querying the database on every cold start, which is the exact 7.5s this replaced
# -- and it would LOOK fine, because the fallback works. `vercel.json`'s own `includeFiles`
# names it too; this exception is what stops it being stripped before that can matter.
!data/deck_snapshot.json.gz
tests/
validation/
migrations/
.claude/
uv.lock
pyproject.toml
.python-version
CLAUDE.md
SPEC.md
CREDITS.md
